    "server_path": "mcp/server.py",
    "server_name": "yol-bulma",
    "tool_name": "skillpack_g005",
    "read_only": true,
    "instructions": "One local deterministic tool. Explain its result and limits; the code decides, a human (usta) approves consequential use. No network access."
  },
  "limitations": "Grids up to 128x128, 64 queries and 200000 search runs per call by default; an 8-second search limit is applied. Uniform tile costs only (no one-way roads, no traffic lights). heuristic_weight > 1 is faster but may return non-shortest paths.",
  "port_notes": "The upstream modules are vendored unmodified (byte-identical to upstream/) under tool/pathfinding; the Skillpack wrapper adds character-to-cost mapping, bounds and blocked-cell checks, grid.cleanup() between queries, cost reporting (end node g) and a time limit of 8 s instead of the upstream 10 s so the pack watchdog never fires first.",
  "flow_role": "Step 2 (rotalar): on the map from G002, compute pedestrian routes on the walk grid and traffic routes on the drive grid, and in step 6 prove every mission target is reachable by car. The paths are embedded in the HTML; the browser never runs A*."
}
